    읕컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴켸

    Some programs make a "video reset" (BIOS function 0) just to clear
    the screen, with the effect, that special character fonts or color
    palettes are destroyed, and the defaults are activated from the VGA
    card.

    XVreset is a memory resident program (TSR), that catches these
    unneccesary resets. XVreset clears the video RAM area instead, and
    resets the cursor.

    XVreset will do this only, when...

    >>   the video mode is not changed by the reset request
    >>   the video system is in 25 lines / 80 columns mode
    >>   not with monochrome monitor
    >>   not in a DOS shell under WINDOWS

    Please test this TSR for those programs that obviously destroy the
    character font. It is suggested to load the TSR (in a BAT file) before
    running the program, and unload it afterwards.

    Option /U to unload. "Load high" as usual.

    Example:
              lh XVreset
              MYPROG
              XVreset /u

    No guarantees - XVreset has not been tested under all possible
    conditions.

